<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-MIM sees new Mt Isa copper costs under 60c/lb.</title>
<headline>RTRS-MIM sees new Mt Isa copper costs under 60c/lb.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>MIM Holdings Ltd said on Sunday it expected production costs from its A$290 million Enterprise copper mine extension at Mount Isa to average less than US$0.60 a pound by about 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;It's high grade, it's deep, but with the technology we have we think we can achieve a very satisfactory cost position at Isa, which I think reflects the quality of that ore body,&quot; MIM's managing director Nick Stump told the Nine Network's Business Sunday programme.</p>
</text>
